rofit_margins":0.136,"net_income":13336000.0,"total_cash":49757000.0,"total_cash_per_share":4.929,"total_debt":4521000.0,"debt_to_equity":5.473,"current_ratio":5.721,"free_cashflow":10383000.0,"return_on_equity":0.15755,"enterprise_value":270971008.0,"enterprise_to_ebitda":16.367,"enterprise_to_revenue":2.763,"earnings_growth":-0.418,"shares_outstanding":10094322.0,"float_shares":3506566.0,"held_pct_insiders":0.65169,"held_pct_institutions":0.30501,"beta":0.456,"fifty_two_week_high":37.92,"fifty_two_week_low":25.58,"fifty_day_average":30.5316,"two_hundred_day_avg":30.9283,"recommendation":"none","all_time_high":193.6,"all_time_low":8.57,"long_business_summary":"Omega Flex, Inc. manufactures and sells flexible metal hoses, fittings, and accessories in the United States, Canada, and internationally. It offers flexible gas piping for use in residential and commercial buildings; fittings; containment pining; and corrugated copper tubing for use in hospitals, ambulatory care centers, dental, physician and veterinary clinics, laboratories, and other facilities. The company sells its products under the TracPipe CSST, CounterStrike CSST, AutoFlare, DoubleTrac, DEF-Trac, and MediTrac brand names. It serves various markets, including construction, manufacturing, transportation, petrochemical, pharmaceutical, and other industries. The company sells its products through independent sales representatives, distributors, wholesalers, original equipment manufacturers, and direct sales, as well as through its website. The company was formerly known as Tofle America, Inc. and changed its name to Omega Flex, Inc. in 1996. Omega Flex, Inc. was incorporated in 1975 and is based in Exton, Pennsylvania."}}